{"title":"03 Assembly: the pipeline","description":"Follow process_dataset from per-file parsing through joined feature frames.","nextTour":"04 Features: 53 measures from text","steps":[{"file":"src/delware_speech/pipeline.py","line":26,"title":"Raw tag → canonical task","description":"`map_to_canonical_task` normalizes a CHAT `@G:` tag through `CANONICAL_PICTURE_TASKS`; anything unrecognized returns None and is dropped from the feature frame."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/pipeline.py","line":35,"title":"One file → N records","description":"`process_single_cha` parses one transcript and emits one record per canonical picture task present (zero or more). This is why the all-tasks frame can hold several rows per participant."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/pipeline.py","line":44,"title":"Header-fallback demographics","description":"`demo_info` starts from the transcript header fields; `Diagnosis` defaults to `Control` when the header has none (line 52) — the silent fallback book/quickstart warns about."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/pipeline.py","line":56,"title":"The demographics join","description":"Exact `ID` match against the workbook rows. Non-null workbook fields overwrite the header fallbacks — so the workbook always wins when a row exists."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/pipeline.py","line":87,"title":"Feature extraction happens here","description":"Per task with non-empty text, `extract_linguistic_features(text)` returns the 63-column dict that is merged into the record (line 102). Tour 04 opens that function up."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/pipeline.py","line":108,"title":"Batch orchestration","description":"`process_dataset(corpus_root, demographics_excel)` walks the corpus, calls the per-file processor under a tqdm bar, and returns the all-tasks DataFrame."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/pipeline.py","line":121,"title":"transcript/ auto-detect","description":"If a `transcript/` subdirectory exists under the corpus root, the search moves into it — Delaware ships transcripts nested one level down."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/pipeline.py","line":129,"title":"Missing workbook is not fatal","description":"A demographics path that doesn't exist is skipped with no error: the run continues on header metadata only. That's the silent-fallback behavior — verify the join happened on real runs."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/pipeline.py","line":140,"title":"Per-file error containment","description":"One malformed transcript logs an error and the batch continues — `process_dataset` never lets a single bad `.cha` kill a corpus run."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/pipeline.py","line":147,"title":"All tasks → one row per person","description":"`select_unique_participants` implements the paper's rule: keep one speech sample per participant, prioritized Cookie > Cat > Rockwell (line 149's `priority` tuple), earliest visit first."},{"file":"src/delware_speech/pipeline.py","line":161,"title":"Priority as a sort key","description":"Tasks map to a rank (Cookie 0, Cat 1, Rockwell 2, unknown 999); lines 171–177 sort by participant → priority → visit number and keep the first row per person."}]}